<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rwandan Revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1959–1961</span> · Also known as Hutu Revolution</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rwandan Revolution, or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hutu">Hutu</a> Revolution, was a period of violence and political change in Rwanda from 1959 to 1961 that ended the Tutsi-led monarchy. Beginning with attacks on Tutsi in November 1959, it brought the Hutu party <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parmehutu">Parmehutu</a> to power with Belgian support, abolished the monarchy in 1961 and drove many Tutsi into exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rwandan-revolution.jpg" alt="Rwandan Revolution" width="256" height="406" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Post of Rwanda · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stamp_of_Rwanda_-_1969_-_Colnect_588946_-_Worker_with_Pickaxe_and_Flag.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
